dossiers.argument_text:
The current federal minimum wage cannot sustain one to live today.Someone could be working full time and they cannot even afford a one bedroom in most parts of the country(2A,A nationwide analysis finds that a full-time worker earning the federal minimum wage cannot afford a modest one-bedroom apartment in most areas of the United States.).Not to mention the other basic needs.anyone working more than 40 hours a week should not be  struggling to survive(2B,A nationwide analysis finds that a full-time worker earning the federal minimum wage cannot afford basic necessities anywhere in the United States.
).                                                            Raising the wages is fair and is a better way of improving peoples lives and living standards of many families out of poverty(1A,A Congressional Budget Office analysis projects that increasing the federal minimum wage would lift hundreds of thousands of people out of poverty.).It is only fair to give them the shot to hardworking people.Current data shows that higher minimun wages will boost income for those who need it the most directly(1B,A study of family incomes finds that higher minimum wages raise incomes near the bottom of the income distribution and reduce poverty among non-elderly households.
).
